@startuml

start

:Automotive ECU operates within safety-critical ISO 26262 framework;
:Orchestrate subsystems via CAN/Ethernet network;
fork
  :Powertrain;
fork again
  :BMS;
fork again
  :Chassis subsystems;
end fork
:Utilize priority-based scheduling managed by RTOS;

if (Anomalous sensor data?) then (yes)
fork
  :Trigger dedicated signal conditioning ISR;
  :Initialize multi-threaded task module;

  fork
    :Time-sliced data acquisition from ring buffer;
  fork again
    :Real-time execution of primary control algorithm;
  end fork

  :Perform CRC-based data verification check;
  if (Successful?) then (yes)
    :Re-initialize module with dedicated threads;
    :Transition to low-power standby state managed by PMIC;
  else (no)
    :Mutex-protected fault handler engages default operating mode;
    :Continuously poll environmental sensors;
  end if

fork again
  :Telemetry monitor driven by hardware timer;
  :Execute in fixed-periodic loop ;
  :Implement exponential backoff for transient faults;
end fork

else (no)
end if

:All system actions time-stamped for persistence;
fork
:UDS/ISO-TP diagnostics and hardware watchdog timer ensure;
fork
:Robust recovery;
fork again
:Managed transitions to limp-home modes;
end fork

stop

@enduml
